@startuml download-export-copy
|User|
start
if (Choose?) then (download project)
  |Editor|
  :Write every block unchanged into one .puml file
  named after the project;
  if (Blocks that cannot be rendered, or not yet checked?) then (yes)
    :Non-blocking notice listing them, saying how many
    are not yet checked and that standard PlantUML
    will report errors for them;
  else (no)
  endif
  if (Screen flow invalid or source-only?) then (yes)
    :Non-blocking notice that the flow will be
    imported as other content if re-imported;
  else (no)
  endif
  |Storage|
  :Record the last-downloaded time and
  clear the "not downloaded" indicator;
elseif (Choose?) then (export SVG or PNG)
  |Editor|
  if (Can the open screen or flow be rendered?) then (yes)
    |Renderer|
    :Render it as SVG;
    if (Render succeeded?) then (yes)
      :For PNG, rasterise the same SVG at 2× size;
      |Editor|
      :Save the image, matching the preview;
    else (no)
      |Editor|
      :Explain the rendering problem; no image is saved;
    endif
  else (no: invalid, older format or depends on !include)
    :Prevent the export and explain why;
    :Source download and copy remain available;
  endif
else (copy source)
  |Editor|
  :Copy the open block's source, or the
  whole project's, to the clipboard;
  :Confirm that it was copied;
endif
|User|
stop
@enduml
